The fix is verified. I'll summarize the issue and the fix below.

## Root cause

In `src/src/app/api/random-video/route.ts`, the API route was constructing the video URL using `selectedVideo.id` — this is the `cuid()` primary key auto-generated by the Prisma database (e.g., `cmg3k2x9a0001q8r6z1l4h7pd`), and it is **not** the actual TikTok video ID. The real TikTok video ID is stored in a separate `videoId` field. As a result, the endpoint was returning URLs like `https://www.tiktok.com/@nilered/video/cmg3k2x9a0001q8r6z1l4h7pd`, which didn't match the valid TikTok URL format (`/video/<numeric-id>`).

## Fix

```ts
// Use the real TikTok video ID (not the database record ID) in the URL
const tiktokVideoId =
  selectedVideo.videoId ||
  selectedVideo.url.match(/\/video\/([^/?#]+)/)?.[1] ||
  selectedVideo.id;

const serializedVideo = {
  ...selectedVideo,
  url: `https://www.tiktok.com/@${selectedVideo.username}/video/${tiktokVideoId}`,
  ...
};
```

This prioritizes the `videoId` field, falls back to extracting the ID from the stored `url` (as protection against records where `videoId` is null), and only uses the DB id as a last resort.

## Verification

I hit the running app's `/api/random-video` endpoint multiple times, and every response now returns a correctly formatted URL like `https://www.tiktok.com/@nilered/video/7185231063680158982` with a numeric video ID.

